3c33c483-384f-479a-827b-a0390e303ead	b0861726-81c3-40c5-ac12-e66c5ec9c4bc	f10ad07d-a91a-4c52-9f54-31b000d3b6f9	assistant	To create a new order for a customer in the CS-ERP system, you'll need to navigate to the Operations module. Here's how:\n\n**Steps to Create a New Order:**\n\n1. **Navigate to Orders** - I can take you directly to the orders page\n2. **Select Customer** - Choose from your existing customer database\n3. **Enter Shipment Details** - Container type, cargo details, weight, etc.\n4. **Set Route** - Origin port, destination port, transit details\n5. **Add Services** - Freight, handling, documentation, customs\n6. **Review & Submit** - Confirm all details before creating the order\n\n**Required Information:**\n- Customer/Shipper details\n- Consignee information\n- Container specifications (20ft, 40ft, HC, etc.)\n- Cargo description and weight\n- Port of loading and discharge\n- Sailing schedule preferences\n- Special requirements (hazardous, temperature controlled, etc.)\n\nWould you like me to take you to the orders creation page now?\n\n\n\nOr do you need help with any specific part of the order creation process?	\N	{"page": "/operations/orders/new", "action": "navigate"}	839	2026-03-07 20:01:34.67421+00	2026-03-16 13:30:26.349127+00	\N	\N	\N
