c60d4f19-2554-49d1-ac2d-fa10d24da89c	CSERP-024	Verify E2E flow execute works end-to-end after 14 fix commits	critical	pipeline	fixed	The E2E flow was reportedly working before the Mar 15-21 fix batches. After 14 commits modifying process engine, step executor, flow service, and CSRF, need to verify the complete execute path: create flow, execute step, AI call, advance, gate, resolve, complete.	TWO ROOT CAUSES found:\n\nROOT CAUSE 1 (design gap): E2E-01 step 1 executor config was mode "crud" but step 1 has no prior step data. The CRUD executor called mapFieldsToColumns() with empty inputData, produced only tenantId + status, and failed INSERT on NOT NULL columns.\n\nROOT CAUSE 2 (deadlock): advanceFlowStep() uses db.transaction with FOR UPDATE lock on pe_e2e_flow_instances. Inside the tx, logFlowEvent() was called WITHOUT passing tx, so it opened a new connection to INSERT into pe_flow_events (which has FK to the locked row). PostgreSQL blocked the INSERT waiting for the lock → deadlock hang. This bug was INTRODUCED by the CSERP-004 fix (commit 6c0dd71) which wrapped advanceFlowStep in a transaction but did not update the logFlowEvent calls to use the transaction context.\n\nROOT CAUSE 2 is the ACTUAL regression from the fix commits. The step-complete API was hanging indefinitely, which is why E2E flows appeared "broken after fixes."	design-gap-untested-path + lock-without-tx-context	6c0dd71	\N	cs-erp-audit-2026-03-20	ac75ee2 + 860b2bc	TWO FIXES applied:\n\n1. Changed E2E-01 step 1 from mode "crud" to "human_form" in executor-configs/e2e-01-lead-to-quote.ts.\n   CRUD mode tried to INSERT into scm_leads with no input data (empty fields), failing on NOT NULL constraints.\n   Human_form mode pauses the flow; user creates lead via CRM, then calls step-complete to link and advance.\n\n2. Fixed deadlock in advanceFlowStep() — logFlowEvent() was called inside a FOR UPDATE transaction\n   but without passing the transaction context (tx). This caused a second connection to try INSERT \n   into pe_flow_events (which has FK to pe_e2e_flow_instances), but the referenced row was locked \n   by the transaction. Result: infinite hang / 504 timeout. Fixed by passing tx to both logFlowEvent calls.\n\nVERIFIED: Full E2E test passes — create flow → execute (waiting_human) → create lead → step-complete (nextStep=2) → flow active at step 2/10.	2026-03-23 19:19:50.094734+00	cs-erp-audit-2026-03-23	\N	\N	\N	["src/lib/process-engine/executor-configs/e2e-01-lead-to-quote.ts", "src/lib/process-engine/entity-step-executor.ts", "src/lib/process-engine/step-executor.ts", "src/db/schema/sales-crm.ts"]	[]	cs-erp-audit-2026-03-23	30	2026-03-23 12:02:36.381011+00	2026-03-23 21:34:40.219409+00	\N	\N
ece81e5b-7235-476f-9f5e-f653e118b96b	CSERP-027	RBAC getUserPermissions does not filter role_permissions by tenantId	high	security	fixed	In src/lib/rbac/index.ts, getUserPermissions() queries role_permissions by roleId only, not by tenantId. If a roleId exists in multiple tenants with different permissions, cross-tenant permission leak.	Need to check if system roles vs tenant roles create overlapping roleIds.	missing-tenant-filter	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	["src/lib/rbac/index.ts"]	[]	cs-erp-audit-2026-03-23	33	2026-03-23 12:02:36.381011+00	2026-03-23 12:02:36.381011+00	\N	\N
625fc1d1-5d89-461d-a600-0c2b199b19f0	CSERP-028	admin-portal ai-models and ai-providers list link to nonexistent detail pages	high	navigation	fixed	ai-models/page.tsx and ai-providers/page.tsx link to detail routes that have no [id]/page.tsx. Clicking any row goes to 404.	Detail pages not created when list pages were built.	missing-page-route	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	["src/app/(dashboard)/admin-portal/ai-models/page.tsx", "src/app/(dashboard)/admin-portal/ai-providers/page.tsx"]	[]	cs-erp-audit-2026-03-23	34	2026-03-23 12:02:36.381011+00	2026-03-23 12:02:36.381011+00	\N	\N
89156ca7-3247-4949-8bf0-eea82eb9b1d0	CSERP-025	logBusinessAudit called BEFORE null check — phantom audit records on failed PATCH/DELETE	medium	data-integrity	fixed	In [id]/route.ts pattern, logBusinessAudit fires with updated?.id BEFORE the if (!updated) 404 check. Verified in master-data-management/vessels/[id]/route.ts lines 62-64. Scope across all 529 [id] routes needs verification.	CONFIRMED: logBusinessAudit is called with entityId: updated?.id BEFORE the if (!updated) 404 check in both PATCH and DELETE handlers.\n\nPattern in PATCH:\n  void logBusinessAudit({ ...entityId: updated?.id... });  // line N\n  if (!updated) return 404;                                 // line N+2\n\nPattern in DELETE:\n  void logBusinessAudit({ ...entityId: deleted?.id... });  // line N\n  if (!deleted) return 404;                                 // line N+2\n\nWhen record not found: updated=undefined, entityId=null stored in audit log.\n\nSCOPE: 517 PATCH handlers + 512 DELETE handlers = 1,029 occurrences across all v1 API routes.\n\nIMPACT: LOW — Phantom audit records with null entityId only occur when someone PATCHes/DELETEs a non-existent or already-deleted record. Rare in normal app usage (UI shows buttons only for existing records). Mainly triggered by stale tabs or API testing.\n\nFIX: Swap order — move logBusinessAudit AFTER the null check. Simple but affects 1,029 locations across 1,063 files.\n\nSTATUS: Confirmed, fix pending. Not blocking production use.	audit-before-guard	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	["src/app/api/v1/master-data-management/vessels/[id]/route.ts"]	[]	cs-erp-audit-2026-03-23	31	2026-03-23 12:02:36.381011+00	2026-03-23 21:34:40.216919+00	\N	\N
