7b5a0b87-c070-42cc-9e78-bb177bc0cb7c	\N	E2E-07-S10	Legal gate: authorize legal action	Authorize commencement of legal proceedings if payment not received after legal notice period. Decision factors: debt amount vs expected legal costs (litigation is expensive — typically only justified for debts >$25,000), customer's financial status (is the customer solvent? No point suing an insolvent company), jurisdiction (enforcing judgments across borders is complex and costly), evidence strength (is our claim well-documented?), and commercial relationship (are we prepared to end this relationship?). Alternatives to litigation: mediation, arbitration (if contract specifies), or debt collection agency. Authority: CFO approval for legal action. Engage external legal counsel for proceedings.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	CFO / Legal Counsel	48.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Legal Notice Response (or lack thereof)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 9 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:9\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Debt Amount vs Estimated Legal Costs\\",\\"source\\":\\"Legal\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Solvency Assessment\\",\\"source\\":\\"Credit Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Evidence Package\\",\\"source\\":\\"Collections File\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Decision (litigate/arbitrate/mediate/collection agency/write-off)\\",\\"Legal Budget Authorized\\",\\"External Counsel Engaged\\",\\"Timeline for Proceedings\\"]"	"[\\"Cost-benefit analysis supports action\\",\\"Customer solvency verified\\",\\"Evidence package complete\\",\\"Budget authorized\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.024789+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.024789+00
6a766f1f-d497-452a-a864-b988bb47e2a9	\N	E2E-07-S13	Payment plan gate: approve installment terms	Approve payment plan for customers in genuine financial difficulty who want to settle but cannot pay in full immediately. Payment plan terms: installment amount and frequency (monthly is standard), total repayment period (typically 3-12 months), interest during plan period (usually charged at contractual or statutory rate), security/guarantee (personal guarantee from director, or bank guarantee for large amounts), and default clause (if customer misses any installment, full balance becomes immediately due). For amounts >$50K: formal written agreement reviewed by legal. While on payment plan: customer may be allowed limited new bookings (on prepayment basis) to maintain relationship. Authority: credit controller up to $25K, finance manager up to $100K, CFO above.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Credit Controller / Finance Manager	24.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Payment Plan Proposal\\",\\"source\\":\\"Customer / Account Manager\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Total Outstanding Amount\\",\\"source\\":\\"AR Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Financial Assessment\\",\\"source\\":\\"Credit Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Payment Plan Template\\",\\"source\\":\\"Legal\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Payment Plan Approved/Rejected\\",\\"Agreed Installment Schedule\\",\\"Interest Rate Applied\\",\\"Security/Guarantee Required\\",\\"Default Clause Terms\\"]"	"[\\"Customer's financial ability assessed\\",\\"Plan is realistic and achievable\\",\\"Security adequate for amount\\",\\"Approval at correct authority\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.030137+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.030137+00
38f49413-0ffb-40a0-ada4-525343260180	\N	E2E-07-S15	Write-off gate: approve bad debt write-off	Approve bad debt write-off for receivables deemed uncollectable after all collection efforts exhausted. Write-off criteria: customer confirmed insolvent/bankrupt (official notice), all dunning levels completed, legal action taken (or cost-benefit analysis shows legal action not viable), credit insurance claim filed and resolved (if insured), and debt aged beyond statutory limitation period. Authority: finance controller up to $10K, finance manager up to $50K, CFO up to $200K, board above $200K. Tax deductibility: ensure documentation meets local tax requirements for bad debt deduction (varies by jurisdiction — Qatar requires evidence of commercial loss, India requires write-off in books + efforts documented). Credit insurance recovery offset against write-off amount.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Finance Manager / CFO / Board	72.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Write-off Request with Justification\\",\\"source\\":\\"Collections\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Collection Effort Documentation\\",\\"source\\":\\"Dunning/Legal Records\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Credit Insurance Claim Status\\",\\"source\\":\\"Insurance Module\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Tax Deductibility Requirements\\",\\"source\\":\\"Tax Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Write-off Approved\\",\\"Approved Amount (net of insurance recovery)\\",\\"Tax Deductible Amount\\",\\"Approval Authority\\",\\"Audit Documentation\\"]"	"[\\"Collection efforts fully documented\\",\\"Insurance recovery offset\\",\\"Tax documentation complete\\",\\"Authority level correct for amount\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.03412+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.03412+00
