3f8bd91d-42cb-4665-8006-661b304d0621	\N	E2E-08-S03	L/C gate: accept or request amendment	Trade finance manager reviews the AI-generated term comparison report and decides whether to accept the L/C as-is or request amendments from the applicant/issuing bank. Decision paths: (1) ACCEPT — L/C terms are compliant, no discrepancies, proceed to tracking and document preparation; (2) AMEND — issue an amendment request (MT707) specifying exact changes needed (amount, dates, document requirements, conditions) — L/C returns to step 1 when amended L/C is received; (3) REJECT — L/C is fundamentally unworkable (wrong beneficiary, sanctioned bank, impossible conditions) — notify sales team and customer. For amendments, the manager drafts the specific amendment language, sends to the advising bank, and tracks the amendment cycle (applicant must agree to amendments). Multiple amendment rounds may be needed. Consider: amendment costs (banks charge per amendment), time impact on shipment schedule, and whether amendment delays risk missing the latest shipment date.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Trade Finance Manager	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Term-by-Term Comparison Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 2 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Discrepancy List with Severity\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 2 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Soft Clause Warnings\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 2 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Amendment Cost Estimate\\",\\"source\\":\\"Bank Fee Schedule\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Gate Decision (Accept/Amend/Reject)\\",\\"Amendment Request Details (if amend)\\",\\"Accepted L/C Confirmation\\",\\"Amendment Tracking Reference\\"]"	"[\\"Decision documented with rationale\\",\\"Amendment request specifies exact clause changes\\",\\"Time impact on shipment assessed if amending\\",\\"Rejection communicated to all stakeholders\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.046774+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.046774+00
5eb9e9c3-3868-4b69-919b-81ba4613f2b1	\N	E2E-08-S08	Document gate: review compliance	Senior trade finance officer performs final manual review of the complete documentary set before bank presentation. This is the last quality gate — once documents are presented to the bank, discrepancies are costly (discrepancy fees typically USD 50-150 per discrepancy, plus delays of 5-15 business days for resolution). Review: (1) Physical inspection of original documents (signatures, stamps, letterheads); (2) Verify AI-generated compliance report — spot-check critical fields; (3) Ensure document set is complete per L/C field 46A checklist; (4) Confirm presentation deadline allows sufficient time (documents must reach bank before L/C expiry and within presentation period); (5) Check if any documents need legalization/apostille (some L/Cs require embassy legalization for certain countries). Approve for presentation or return with specific corrections needed.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Senior Trade Finance Officer	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Complete Document Set Package\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Cross-Document Consistency Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"L/C Presentation Deadline Countdown\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 4 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Document Checklist with Status\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 Output\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Gate Decision (Approve/Return for Corrections)\\",\\"Corrections Required (if returned)\\",\\"Presentation Authorization\\",\\"Courier Instructions for Original Documents\\"]"	"[\\"All original documents physically present and signed\\",\\"Presentation deadline achievable with courier transit time\\",\\"No legalization requirements outstanding\\",\\"Document count matches L/C specified quantities\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.052893+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.052893+00
8eabf7b0-95a7-4fba-a999-fc77a465274c	\N	E2E-08-S11	Discrepancy gate: amend L/C or accept	Trade finance manager reviews the discrepancy analysis and decides the resolution path. Options: (1) CORRECT AND RE-PRESENT — authorize document corrections, track re-presentation deadline; (2) REQUEST WAIVER — instruct bank to send cable waiver request to applicant, await response; (3) AMEND L/C — request L/C amendment to cover discrepancies (requires applicant consent); (4) PRESENT UNDER RESERVE — accept risk that applicant may refuse payment; (5) FALL BACK TO COLLECTION — convert to documentary collection basis (D/P or D/A). Critical decision factors: relationship with applicant (will they waive?), remaining L/C validity, cargo status (already discharged?), amount at risk, and whether discrepancies are technical or substantive. If cargo is already at destination and buyer needs it, waiver is likely. If buyer has market price advantage to refuse, risk is higher.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Trade Finance Manager	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Discrepancy Analysis Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 10 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Resolution Strategy Recommendations\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 10 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Relationship History\\",\\"source\\":\\"CRM Module\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Cargo Discharge Status\\",\\"source\\":\\"Operations Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Resolution Decision (Correct/Waiver/Amend/Reserve/Collection)\\",\\"Instructions to Bank\\",\\"Revised Payment Timeline\\",\\"Risk Acceptance (if presenting under reserve)\\"]"	"[\\"Decision documented with risk assessment rationale\\",\\"Bank instructions issued within refusal notice response period\\",\\"Sales team notified if waiver request sent to customer\\",\\"Cash flow forecast updated for revised timeline\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.057544+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.057544+00
