890cb066-716b-42b2-b37e-ffbc076d7d84	\N	E2E-16-S13	Damage gate: agree M&R liability	Agree on M&R (maintenance and repair) liability between lessee and lessor. Common disputes: whether damage is 'normal wear' (lessor bears) or 'lessee damage' (lessee bears). IICL repair standards provide guidelines but gray areas exist (e.g., floor scuffing from normal cargo loading vs forklift damage). For each damage item: agree liability, repair method, and cost. If DPP was elected: submit eligible damage items under DPP coverage. Negotiate if lessor's repair cost estimate seems excessive (common with lessor-controlled depots). Document agreed liability split for final settlement calculation.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Equipment Manager / Lessor Representative	48.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Off-hire Survey Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 12 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:12\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"IICL Liability Guidelines\\",\\"source\\":\\"Standards Database\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"DPP Terms (if elected)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Lease Agreement\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Historical M&R Costs (similar damage)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Maintenance Module\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Agreed Liability Split (lessee/lessor/DPP)\\",\\"Lessee M&R Cost\\",\\"DPP Claim Amount\\",\\"Disputed Items (if any)\\",\\"Agreed Repair Method\\"]"	"[\\"All damage items addressed\\",\\"IICL standards referenced for each item\\",\\"DPP claims submitted within terms\\",\\"Liability split documented and agreed\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.294073+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.294073+00
