dced2d4f-c376-448e-86cd-172e2a57cc94	\N	E2E-17-S02	D&D tariff lookup by port/customer/contract	Look up the applicable demurrage and detention tariff rates. Tariff hierarchy (highest priority first): 1) customer-specific contract rate, 2) trade lane rate agreement, 3) port-specific tariff, 4) global default tariff. Tariffs are structured as tiered rates — e.g., days 1-5 at $50/day, days 6-10 at $75/day, days 11+ at $100/day. Rates vary by: container size (20'/40'/45'), container type (dry/reefer/tank/flat-rack), port, and currency. For multi-currency operations: rates stored in local currency with conversion to billing currency at invoice date rate.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a D&D Tariff Agent. Look up applicable D&D tariff rates by port, customer, and contract. Apply tiered rates (days 1-5, 6-10, 11+). Provide JSON with: demurrageRate, detentionRate, tiers, contractOverride.\\"}"	\N	D&D Tariff AI Agent	0.50	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Port Code\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:1\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer ID\\",\\"source\\":\\"Booking / BL\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Container Size and Type\\",\\"source\\":\\"Equipment Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Contract Reference (if exists)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Contract Module\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Trade Lane\\",\\"source\\":\\"Booking Module\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Applicable Tariff ID\\",\\"Rate Tiers (days → rate/day)\\",\\"Currency\\",\\"Tariff Source (contract/trade/port/default)\\",\\"Maximum Charge Cap (if any)\\"]"	"[\\"Tariff hierarchy correctly applied\\",\\"Rate tiers are complete and non-overlapping\\",\\"Currency matches billing requirements\\",\\"Contract rate expiry checked\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.304768+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.304768+00
603a2db1-9aea-4bb8-8737-428078ec4f2a	\N	E2E-17-S03	D&D charge calculation	Calculate total demurrage and detention charges per container. Apply tiered tariff rates to chargeable days: multiply each day (or group of days within a tier) by the applicable rate. Handle: partial days (most ports charge full day for any part of a day), combined D&D (single charge covering terminal + outside terminal), split D&D (separate demurrage and detention line items), reefer power charges (additional per-day charge for plugged-in reefers), and hazmat surcharges. For multi-container shipments: calculate per container, summarize per BL. Round per tariff rules (typically to nearest whole currency unit).	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a D&D Charge Calculator. Calculate total D&D charges. Provide JSON with: demurrageAmount, detentionAmount, totalCharges, breakdown.\\"}"	\N	D&D Calculation AI Agent	1.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Chargeable Days\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:1\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Applicable Tariff Tiers\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 2 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:2\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Container Count per BL\\",\\"source\\":\\"Booking / BL\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Reefer Power Status (if applicable)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Terminal System\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Hazmat Classification (if applicable)\\",\\"source\\":\\"DG Module\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Demurrage Amount per Container\\",\\"Detention Amount per Container\\",\\"Reefer Power Charges\\",\\"Total D&D per BL\\",\\"Charge Breakdown by Tier\\",\\"Currency\\"]"	"[\\"Tier boundaries correctly applied\\",\\"Partial day rules followed\\",\\"Reefer power charges match plugged-in days\\",\\"Total reconciles to sum of line items\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.308012+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.308012+00
964c52b3-211f-448c-8129-244c60306bb7	\N	E2E-17-S06	Customer notification with gate event proof	Send D&D invoice notification to customer with full supporting evidence. Notification includes: invoice PDF, charge breakdown summary, gate event timestamps and proof photos (if available), free time calculation showing how chargeable days were determined, applicable tariff reference, and payment instructions. Send via customer's preferred channel (email, portal notification, EDI 997). For large customers: send to designated D&D contact (not general booking contact). Include dispute/query instructions and deadline for dispute submission (typically 14-30 days from invoice date).	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a D&D Notification Agent. Notify customer of D&D charges with gate event proof attached. Provide JSON with: notificationSent, customerRef, attachments, responseDeadline.\\"}"	\N	Notification AI Agent	1.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"D&D Invoice\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 4 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:4\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Contact (D&D designated)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Customer Master\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Gate Event Proof Documents\\",\\"source\\":\\"Terminal System\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Communication Preference\\",\\"source\\":\\"Customer Master\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Dispute Submission Deadline\\",\\"source\\":\\"D&D Policy\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Notification Sent Confirmation\\",\\"Delivery Channel Used\\",\\"Dispute Deadline Communicated\\",\\"Read Receipt (if email)\\"]"	"[\\"All supporting documents attached\\",\\"Correct customer contact used\\",\\"Dispute deadline clearly stated\\",\\"Delivery confirmation received\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.311993+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.311993+00
09087bf3-b3bd-475f-9917-e5a3e2618bf7	\N	E2E-17-S07	Customer dispute received?	System monitors for customer disputes against D&D invoices. Disputes can be submitted via: customer portal (self-service dispute form), email to D&D team, EDI message, or customer service ticket. Dispute must include: invoice reference, disputed amount, reason code (incorrect free time, wrong tariff applied, force majeure, terminal delay, customs hold not customer's fault, etc.), and supporting evidence. System categorizes disputes by: reason code, amount, customer tier, and whether within dispute deadline. Auto-reject if past dispute deadline. Route valid disputes to waiver gate.	\N	system	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Dispute Detection Agent. Check if customer has filed a dispute against D&D charges. Provide JSON with: disputeFiled, disputeReason, disputedAmount.\\"}"	\N	D&D System	0.50	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Invoice Reference\\",\\"source\\":\\"Customer Submission\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Disputed Amount\\",\\"source\\":\\"Customer Submission\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Dispute Reason Code\\",\\"source\\":\\"Customer Submission\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Supporting Evidence\\",\\"source\\":\\"Customer Submission\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Dispute Deadline\\",\\"source\\":\\"Invoice Terms\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Dispute Registered (Y/N)\\",\\"Dispute Reference Number\\",\\"Reason Category\\",\\"Amount Disputed\\",\\"Within Deadline (Y/N)\\"]"	"[\\"Dispute references valid invoice\\",\\"Deadline check performed\\",\\"Reason code is from approved list\\",\\"Evidence attached if required by policy\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.315835+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.315835+00
c4236170-aea5-4487-a1e7-b333fbeb491a	\N	E2E-17-S08	Waiver gate: AI recommends waive/enforce	AI analyzes the dispute and recommends waive or enforce. Analysis considers: customer history (repeat disputes, payment behavior, total revenue value), dispute merit (was the delay actually caused by terminal, customs, or force majeure?), gate event evidence (do timestamps support the customer's claim?), commercial relationship value (is this a top-20 customer by revenue?), and precedent (similar disputes resolved previously). AI generates recommendation with confidence score. For high-confidence recommendations (>90%) on small amounts (<$500): auto-approve the recommendation. For all others: human reviews AI recommendation and makes final decision. Waivers tracked for pattern analysis.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	D&D Controller / Commercial Manager	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Dispute Details\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:7\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"AI Waiver Recommendation\\",\\"source\\":\\"AI Analysis\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Revenue Ranking\\",\\"source\\":\\"CRM\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Dispute History\\",\\"source\\":\\"D&D Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Gate Event Evidence\\",\\"source\\":\\"Terminal System\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Decision (waive/partial waive/enforce)\\",\\"Waiver Amount (if waived)\\",\\"Reason for Decision\\",\\"Approver Name\\"]"	"[\\"Decision documented with rationale\\",\\"Waiver amount within authority limit\\",\\"Customer notified of outcome\\",\\"Pattern analysis updated\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.319464+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.319464+00
