c9e51da7-2607-4034-9485-e56cd551de0f	\N	E2E-24-S04	Market entry decision: proceed with service design or defer/reject	Executive decision gate where senior commercial and strategy leadership reviews the complete market analysis package — trade lane demand forecast, competitive landscape assessment, and P&L projection — and decides whether to proceed with service design. Decision options: (1) Proceed — market opportunity is attractive, P&L is viable, competitive position is achievable; (2) Defer — market timing is not right (e.g., pending port infrastructure completion, regulatory change, alliance restructuring), revisit in 3-6 months; (3) Reject — insufficient demand, overcrowded competitive landscape, or negative P&L even under optimistic scenario. Decision criteria typically include: minimum 3-year NPV positive under base case, break-even load factor achievable within 6 months of service launch, addressable volume sufficient for at least weekly service frequency, and strategic alignment with company trade lane portfolio (avoid cannibalization of existing services). If proceeding, the gate output also defines: target service frequency (weekly/fortnightly), target vessel size range (feeder 1,000-3,000 TEU, regional 3,000-8,000 TEU, mainline 8,000-24,000 TEU), and budget envelope for the service design phase.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Chief Commercial Officer / VP Strategy	48.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Trade Lane Demand Analysis Report (from step 1)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Market Intelligence Agent (Step 1)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Competitive Landscape Assessment (from step 2)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Commercial Intelligence Agent (Step 2)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Trade Lane P&L Projection (from step 3)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Trade Lane P&L Agent (Step 3)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Company Trade Lane Portfolio (existing services for cannibalization check)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Network Planning\\",\