bc0d3cf5-5cf8-45a3-a983-c010001ab7dc	\N	E2E-24-S09	Service design approval: approve port rotation, frequency, alliance terms	Approval gate for the completed service design package. Decision-makers review the final service configuration: confirmed port rotation, service frequency, vessel count requirement, vessel size class, first sailing target, alliance/VSA terms (if applicable), and updated P&L reflecting the specific rotation economics. Approval criteria: (1) Port rotation is operationally feasible and commercially attractive — covers major cargo origin/destination points on the trade lane; (2) Frequency is competitive — matches or exceeds competitor frequency on the route; (3) Vessel requirement is affordable — fleet deployment cost within approved budget envelope from step 4; (4) Alliance/VSA terms are commercially fair — slot costs are market-competitive, utilization commitments are achievable; (5) Updated P&L remains positive under base case. If approved, the service design is locked — any changes after this point require a formal modification request. The gate output authorizes fleet deployment to begin (step 10).	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Chief Commercial Officer / VP Operations	24.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Service Loop Record (code, rotation, frequency, vessel count)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Service Loop Creation (Step 7)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Port Pair Economics Summary (from step 6)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Port Pair Analysis (Step 6)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"VSA Agreement Terms (if applicable, from step 8)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Alliance Negotiation (Step 8)\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Updated Service P&L (reflecting rotation-specific costs)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Trade Lane P&L (Step 3, refined)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Budget Envelope from Market Entry Decision\\",\\"source\\":\\"Market Entry Gate (Step 4)\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Service Design Approval Statu