3ccb562d-802b-4f97-82e2-52ce3fbf9222	\N	E2E-24-S13	Fleet financial assessment (TCE, break-even)	Perform comprehensive fleet financial assessment for the confirmed vessel deployment. Calculate Time Charter Equivalent (TCE) — the industry-standard metric for comparing vessel earnings: TCE = (Gross Revenue − Voyage Costs) / Operating Days. Voyage costs include: bunker (largest variable cost — calculate consumption at eco-speed per leg × bunker price), port charges (pilotage, towage, berth hire per port call), canal dues (Suez Canal tolls based on SCNT measurement, typically $200,000-$700,000 per transit for container vessels), terminal handling costs, and agency fees. For each vessel (owned and chartered): calculate daily operating cost (owned: depreciation + OPEX + finance cost; chartered: hire rate), daily break-even revenue requirement, and break-even load factor. Model fleet-level economics: total deployment cost per round voyage, revenue per round voyage at target utilization, contribution to company overhead, and payback period for repositioning investment. Compare TCE against market TC rates — if TCE < market TC rate, the vessel earns less than if it were chartered out, flagging potential misallocation. Produce fleet deployment financial summary for the approval gate.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Fleet Financial Agent. Assess fleet economics — TCE, break-even, daily costs. Provide JSON with: tcePerDay, breakEvenRate, dailyOpex, annualCost.\\"}"	\N	Fleet Financial Agent	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel Assignment Plan (own + chartered vessels with costs)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Fleet Deployment (Steps 11-12)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Bunker Consumption per Vessel at Eco-Speed (MT/day)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Vessel Particulars / Noon Reports\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Bunker Prices (IFO380, VLSFO, LSMGO by bunkering port)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Ship & Bunker / Procurement\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Port Cost Estimates per Port Call\\",\\"source\\":\\"Port Cost Database / Agent Quotes\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Canal Dues Calculation (SCNT tonnage × tariff)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Canal Authority Tariff\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Revenue Forecast per Round Voyage (from P&L step 3, refined)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Trade Lane P&L\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel Capital Costs (depreciation, finance) or Charter Hire Rate\\",\\"source\\":\\"Finance / Charter Records\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"TCE per Vessel ($/day)\\",\\"Daily Break-Even Revenue per Vessel\\",\\"Break-Even Load Factor per Vessel and Service Average (%)\\",\\"Total Deployment Cost per Round Voyage (bunker + port + canal + vessel cost)\\",\\"Revenue per Round Voyage at Target Utilization\\",\\"Fleet Deployment Financial Summary (cost, revenue, margin per voyage)\\",\\"TCE vs Market TC Rate Comparison (deployment efficiency check)\\",\\"Repositioning Cost Payback Period\\"]"	"[\\"Bunker consumption uses vessel-specific SFOC curves (not fleet average)\\",\\"Port costs based on actual tariffs or recent agent quotes (not estimates)\\",\\"Canal dues calculated using correct SCNT tonnage and current tariff\\",\\"TCE calculation follows industry standard formula\\",\\"Break-even load factor is achievable (typically 50-65%)\\",\\"TCE exceeds market TC rate (vessel deployment more profitable than chartering out)\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.547618+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.547618+00
beb40d77-5d3e-4509-8a63-70cf1bade53a	\N	E2E-24-S14	Fleet deployment approval: vessel assignments, charter decisions, cost commitment	Approval gate for the fleet deployment plan. Decision-makers review: named vessel assignments (own fleet), charter-in commitments (vessels, hire rates, periods), fleet financial assessment (TCE, break-even, cost per voyage), repositioning plan and cost, and comparison against the approved budget envelope from step 4. Approval criteria: (1) All vessels meet technical specification — no compromises on safety-critical parameters (draft, speed); (2) Charter hire rates are market-competitive — within ±10% of current market rates; (3) Break-even load factor is achievable within 3 months of service launch; (4) Total deployment cost within approved budget envelope; (5) TCE exceeds market TC rate (own vessels) — confirms deployment is value-creating. If charter costs exceed budget, options: (a) negotiate harder, (b) reduce vessel count (switch from weekly to fortnightly), (c) defer service launch, or (d) request additional budget. Approval commits significant OPEX (charter hire) and locks fleet capacity — this is the point of no return for fleet allocation.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	VP Fleet Operations / CFO	24.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel Assignment Plan (own fleet)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Fleet Deployment (Step 11)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Charter Commitments (if any, from step 12)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Charter-In (Step 12)\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Fleet Financial Assessment (TCE, break-even, cost summary)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Fleet Financials (Step 13)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Repositioning Plan and Cost\\",\\"source\\":\\"Fleet Deployment (Step 11)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Budget Envelope from Market Entry Decision\\",\\"source\\":\\"Market Entry Gate (Step 4)\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Fleet Deployment Approval Status (approved/rejected