6f91d72b-053a-4148-819c-8b112abd8a84	\N	E2E-24-S29	Load factor reporting & revenue analysis	Generate comprehensive load factor and revenue analysis reports per sailing and per service period. Load factor (utilization %) is the primary commercial performance metric: load_factor = actual_laden_TEU / vessel_effective_capacity × 100. Report per sailing: load factor by direction (head-haul typically 70-90%, back-haul 30-60%), by container type (dry, reefer, special), by port pair segment (which legs are full, which are underutilized), and by customer segment (contract vs spot vs alliance). Revenue analysis per sailing: actual freight revenue per TEU vs budget, surcharge revenue realization (how much of published surcharges actually collected), ancillary revenue (D&D, documentation, weighing fees), and total revenue per round voyage. Calculate unit economics: revenue per TEU, cost per TEU (from fleet financials step 13), contribution margin per TEU, and break-even comparison (actual load factor vs break-even from step 13). Identify trends: load factor trend over trailing 13 weeks, revenue per TEU trend (pricing power indicator), reefer utilization trend, and top/bottom 5 port pairs by contribution margin. Generate management dashboards: weekly commercial performance summary, monthly P&L comparison (actual vs budget from step 3), and quarterly service review deck. Flag financial concerns: if actual load factor is consistently below break-even for 4+ consecutive weeks, trigger escalation for service review (step 31).	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Load Factor Agent. Report load factor and revenue per TEU per voyage. Provide JSON with: loadFactor, revenuePerTeu, voyageRevenue.\\"}"	\N	Revenue Analytics Agent	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Actual Cargo Manifests per Sailing (laden TEU by container type, direction, port pair)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Operations / Stowage Data\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Revenue Records per Sailing (freight + surcharges + ancillary)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Finance / Billing Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel Effective Capacity per Sailing\\",\\"source\\":\\"Capacity Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Budget/Forecast per Sailing (from P&L step 3, demand forecast step 28)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Financial Planning\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Break-Even Load Factor per Vessel (from step 13)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Fleet Financials (Step 13)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Booking Data (segment: contract/spot/alliance)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Booking Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Load Factor per Sailing (overall, by direction, by container type, by segment)\\",\\"Revenue per TEU per Sailing (freight + surcharges + ancillary)\\",\\"Cost per TEU per Sailing (from fleet financials, allocated)\\",\\"Contribution Margin per TEU per Sailing\\",\\"Load Factor Trend (trailing 13 weeks)\\",\\"Revenue per TEU Trend (pricing power indicator)\\",\\"Top/Bottom 5 Port Pairs by Contribution Margin\\",\\"Actual vs Budget P&L Comparison (monthly)\\",\\"Break-Even Compliance Flag (actual LF vs break-even LF)\\"]"	"[\\"Load factor calculated for every completed sailing (no gaps in reporting)\\",\\"Revenue per TEU includes all revenue components (freight + surcharges + ancillary)\\",\\"Actual vs budget variance explained for deviations > 10%\\",\\"Break-even flag triggers when actual LF < break-even LF for 4+ weeks\\",\\"Trend analysis uses minimum 8 data points (8 weeks of sailings)\\",\\"Management dashboard updated weekly by Monday 09:00 local time\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.59733+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.59733+00
baaf1117-d13d-4ec4-9d02-ec76de3bbf02	\N	E2E-24-S30	Route optimization analysis (monthly)	Monthly analysis of route optimization opportunities based on accumulated operational data. After 3-6 months of service operation, sufficient data exists to validate or challenge the original service design assumptions. Analyze: (1) Port call value — for each port on the rotation, calculate the net contribution (revenue generated from cargo loaded/discharged minus port costs, terminal charges, and time cost of the port call). Identify ports where net contribution is negative — candidates for port omission or reduced frequency; (2) Transit time optimization — based on actual speed and weather data, identify legs where schedule can be tightened (faster transit, shorter port stay) or needs relaxation (add buffer where delays are frequent); (3) Port addition opportunities — based on bookings that are being transshipped (indicating demand from non-direct ports), identify ports that could be added to the rotation to capture direct cargo; (4) Seasonal schedule adjustment — analyze seasonal volume patterns and recommend: summer schedule (potentially add port call during peak), winter schedule (potentially omit low-volume port, slow-steam to save bunker); (5) Competition response — if competitor has launched/withdrawn service on overlapping route, recommend adjustments. Output a monthly route optimization report with recommended modifications ranked by financial impact.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Route Optimization Agent. Monthly route optimization analysis — speed, port calls, capacity. Provide JSON with: optimizations, savingsEstimate, recommendations.\\"}"	\N	Route Optimization Agent	16.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Port Call Contribution Analysis (revenue vs cost per port, from step 29)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Load Factor Reporting (Step 29)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Schedule Performance Data (delays by port, from step 27)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Performance Monitoring (Step 27)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Transshipment Cargo Analysis (origin-destination of TS cargo)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Booking / Operations Data\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Seasonal Volume Patterns (monthly volume by port)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Commercial Analytics\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Competitor Service Changes (new services, withdrawals, modifications)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Market Intelligence\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Bunker Cost Trend (for slow steaming / speed adjustment analysis)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Ship & Bunker / Procurement\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Port Call Contribution Ranking (most to least profitable port calls)\\",\\"Port Omission Candidates (negative contribution or marginal value)\\",\\"Port Addition Opportunities (based on TS cargo origin-destination analysis)\\",\\"Transit Time Optimization Recommendations (tighten/relax per leg)\\",\\"Seasonal Schedule Adjustment Proposal (summer/winter schedules)\\",\\"Competition Response Recommendations\\",\\"Financial Impact Estimate per Recommended Modification ($)\\"]"	"[\\"Analysis based on minimum 8 weeks of operational data (meaningful sample)\\",\\"Port contribution calculation includes time cost (opportunity cost of port stay hours)\\",\\"Transshipment analysis traces cargo to actual origin-destination (not just load/discharge port)\\",\\"Financial impact estimates use current rates and costs (not initial P&L assumptions)\\",\\"Recommendations are actionable and include implementation timeline\\",\\"Competitor data is current (checked within last 30 days)\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.601776+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.601776+00
f0aec7b8-44c4-433c-9a52-c07b138284fb	\N	E2E-31-S13	FuelEU Maritime compliance check	Assess compliance with FuelEU Maritime Regulation (EU 2023/1805) which sets GHG intensity limits for energy used on board ships. FuelEU applies from 2025 with progressive reduction targets: -2% by 2025, -6% by 2030, -14.5% by 2035, -31% by 2040, -62% by 2045, -80% by 2050 (vs 2020 reference value of 91.16 gCO2e/MJ). Calculate: (1) GHG intensity of energy used — total well-to-wake GHG emissions / total energy consumed, on a per-MJ basis; (2) Compliance balance — positive (below limit) or negative (above limit, requires action); (3) Flexibility mechanisms — banking (carry forward surplus to next year), borrowing (use future compliance, limited to 2%), pooling (combine compliance balances across fleet or with other companies); (4) Penalty calculation — if non-compliant after flexibilities, penalty = (non-compliant energy in MJ) × (GHG intensity gap) × €2,400 penalty factor; (5) Shore power requirement — from 2030, container ships at EU ports must use onshore power supply (OPS) or equivalent zero-emission technology at berth.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	FuelEU Compliance AI Agent	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Well-to-Wake Emission Data per Fuel Type\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 2 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Total Energy Consumed (MJ) per Vessel\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"FuelEU GHG Intensity Limit (current year)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Regulatory Reference\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Prior Year Compliance Balance (for banking)\\",\\"source\\":\\"ESG Module\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Shore Power Availability at EU Ports\\",\\"source\\":\\"Port Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"GHG Intensity per Vessel (gCO2e/MJ)\\",\\"Compliance Balance (surplus/deficit)\\",\\"Flexibility Mechanism Application\\",\\"Penalty Exposure Calculation\\",\\"Shore Power Compliance Status\\",\\"FuelEU Compliance Certificate Status\\"]"	"[\\"Well-to-wake factors correctly applied per FuelEU methodology\\",\\"Compliance balance uses correct annual GHG intensity limit\\",\\"Flexibility mechanisms applied within regulatory limits\\",\\"Shore power requirement assessed for container ships at EU ports from 2030\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.831373+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.831373+00
9180b554-f071-4dd0-84c1-df35b1f7d2a0	\N	E2E-24-S31	Service review: continue, modify, suspend, or retire	Periodic service review gate (quarterly or triggered by performance alerts) where senior management decides the service's future. Review the complete performance package: schedule reliability trend, load factor trend, revenue per TEU trend, actual vs budget P&L, route optimization recommendations, demand forecast outlook, and competitive landscape changes. Decision options: (1) Continue unchanged — service is performing at or above expectations, no modifications needed; (2) Modify — implement specific changes such as port addition/omission, frequency change (weekly to fortnightly or vice versa), vessel swap (larger/smaller based on demand), rate adjustment, or rotation resequencing. Modification requires formal change request flowing back through relevant steps (network design, terminal negotiation, schedule revision); (3) Suspend — temporarily halt the service due to seasonal low demand, geopolitical disruption (e.g., Red Sea/Houthi crisis forcing Suez Canal avoidance in 2024-2025), or vessel reallocation to higher-priority service. Suspension maintains service identity for restart; (4) Retire — permanently discontinue the service. Triggers: customer notification (minimum 30-60 days advance), booking rundown (stop accepting new bookings, honor existing), final voyage execution, terminal agreement termination, rate withdrawal, and capacity reallocation. This gate may also make ad-hoc decisions: blank sailing (cancel a specific sailing due to low demand — save bunker/port costs), extra loader (add a sailing due to overflow demand), or port omission (skip a port on specific voyage due to congestion/weather).	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	CCO / VP Operations / CEO (for retirement decision)	48.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Schedule Reliability Report (from step 27)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Performance Monitoring (Step 27)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Load Factor and Revenue Analysis (from step 29)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Revenue Analysis (Step 29)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Demand Forecast Outlook (from step 28)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Demand Forecasting (Step 28)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Route Optimization Recommendations (from step 30)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Route Optimization (Step 30)\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Competitive Landscape Update\\",\\"source\\":\\"Market Intelligence\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Actual vs Budget P&L (cumulative since launch)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Finance / Revenue Analysis\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Service Decision: Continue / Modify / Suspend / Retire\\",\\"Modification Details (if modify — specific changes and implementation plan)\\",\\"Suspension Terms (if suspend — duration, restart conditions, customer notification plan)\\",\\"Retirement Plan (if retire — rundown schedule, customer notification, final voyage)\\",\\"Ad-Hoc Decisions (blank sailing, extra loader, port omission for specific voyages)\\",\\"Next Review Date\\"]"	"[\\"Decision based on minimum 1 quarter of operational data (not premature judgment)\\",\\"Financial assessment includes actual vs budget comparison with variance explanation\\",\\"Customer notification plan in place for suspend/retire decisions (30-60 day advance)\\",\\"Modification decision flows back to relevant steps (design, terminal, schedule) for implementation\\",\\"Next review date set (quarterly cycle or earlier if performance-triggered)\\",\\"Decision documented with rationale and named decision-makers\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.606369+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.606369+00
