bd8ac0c3-4d0c-4346-a991-aacf1f4f68dc	\N	E2E-25-S07	Journal gate: dual authorization on manual journals	Dual authorization for manual journal entries as required by internal controls. Auto-generated journals (depreciation, standard accruals) are pre-approved by system. Manual journals require: preparer (cannot be the same as approver), first approver (finance controller or equivalent), and second approver for journals above threshold (typically >$50,000 or involving unusual accounts). Review checks: journal description is adequate, account codes are correct, amounts are supported by calculation, and the journal makes business sense. For adjusting entries: verify they correct a specific identified error. For reclassification entries: verify the transfer is appropriate. Audit trail preserved for all approvals.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Finance Controller / Finance Manager	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Manual Journal Entries for Approval\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 6 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:6\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Supporting Documentation per Journal\\",\\"source\\":\\"Preparers\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"DOA Matrix (authorization limits)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Policy\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Journals Approved\\",\\"Journals Rejected (with reason)\\",\\"Journals Modified\\",\\"Approval Audit Trail\\"]"	"[\\"Dual authorization completed\\",\\"Segregation of duties maintained\\",\\"Supporting docs adequate\\",\\"Unusual journals flagged for review\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.621651+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.621651+00
dd688409-fba0-43c6-8db7-30ba68a5c6f2	\N	E2E-25-S10	Intercompany elimination entries	Generate intercompany elimination entries for consolidated reporting. Identify and eliminate: intercompany revenue/expenses (services between group entities — e.g., Qatar head office charges management fees to UAE and India subsidiaries), intercompany receivables/payables (must net to zero at group level), intercompany profit in inventory (if one entity sells goods/services to another at markup), and intercompany dividends. For each intercompany pair: verify balances agree (both sides record the same amount — if not, identify timing differences or errors). Post elimination entries to consolidation adjustments ledger (not to individual entity books). Handle: different functional currencies between entities (elimination in group reporting currency).	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Consolidation AI Agent	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Intercompany Transaction Register\\",\\"source\\":\\"Multi-entity Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Entity-level GL Balances\\",\\"source\\":\\"GL Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Intercompany Receivable/Payable Balances\\",\\"source\\":\\"AR/AP Modules\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Group Reporting Currency Rates\\",\\"source\\":\\"Treasury\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Intercompany Elimination Entries\\",\\"Balance Matching Report (per entity pair)\\",\\"Timing Differences Identified\\",\\"Consolidation Adjustments\\"]"	"[\\"All intercompany pairs balanced\\",\\"Eliminations net to zero\\",\\"Currency translation correct\\",\\"Intercompany profit eliminated\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.626699+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.626699+00
