6f1737ac-51e2-428a-8b79-36711793db12	\N	E2E-27-S04	Bunkering gate: approve port and quantity	Approve bunkering plan (port, quantity, estimated cost). Bunker manager reviews: is the recommended port the best option considering current market conditions? Is the quantity sufficient with safety margin? Is the port stay long enough for bunkering operations? Are there any operational or safety concerns at the recommended port? For large stem purchases (>1,000 MT): additional review of market timing (should we buy now or wait for price to drop?). Approve budget based on estimated cost (typically bunker price × quantity × 1.05 for contingency). Authority: bunker manager for standard purchases, VP Operations for purchases >$500K or at non-standard ports.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Bunker Manager / VP Operations	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Bunkering Plan Recommendation\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 3 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:3\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Current Market Price Trend\\",\\"source\\":\\"Bunker Market Data\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Budget vs Actual YTD (bunker spend)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Finance\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Bunkering Plan Approved\\",\\"Approved Port and Quantity\\",\\"Budget Authorization\\",\\"Market Timing Decision (buy now/wait)\\"]"	"[\\"Plan reviewed against alternatives\\",\\"Budget authorized\\",\\"Quantity includes safety margin\\",\\"Approval at correct authority level\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.699927+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.699927+00
c24b09db-5159-423c-9bc2-a6be704e1cde	\N	E2E-27-S07	Supplier gate: approve PO award	Approve bunker supplier selection and authorize PO. Bunker manager confirms: recommended supplier is the best value, price is at or below market benchmark, supplier has no outstanding quality or delivery issues, and delivery window fits vessel schedule. For high-value stems (>$300K): VP Operations co-approval. For emergency bunkering (vessel critical on fuel): expedited approval process (phone confirmation, documented post-facto). Award decision communicated to supplier immediately (bids are time-sensitive — prices may change within hours).	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Bunker Manager / VP Operations	2.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Bid Evaluation Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 6 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:6\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel Schedule Constraints\\",\\"source\\":\\"Operations\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Supplier Approved\\",\\"PO Authorization\\",\\"Delivery Window Confirmed\\",\\"Price Locked\\"]"	"[\\"Price at or below benchmark\\",\\"Supplier has clean quality record\\",\\"Delivery fits schedule\\",\\"Authority level correct\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.705209+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.705209+00
b1802141-f9d2-421b-ab59-0421202b0e2f	\N	E2E-28-S03	Match found?	Analyze screening results to determine if any actionable matches exist that require human investigation. This is the triage step that filters false positives from genuine matches to avoid overwhelming investigators with low-quality alerts. Process: (1) Aggregate all matches from customer and vendor screening; (2) Apply secondary filters — compare match details beyond name: date of birth, nationality, address, passport number (where available in sanctions list entries); (3) Cross-reference against previously investigated and cleared matches (cleared matches are retained for 12 months before requiring re-investigation); (4) De-duplicate — same entity may appear in multiple sanctions lists, consolidate into single investigation case; (5) Prioritize — rank matches by: match score, sanctions program severity (OFAC primary > secondary, EU blocking > reporting), financial exposure (amount of business with matched entity), and operational urgency (is there an active booking/payment pending). Route: exact matches → immediate investigation, strong matches → investigation within 24 hours, possible matches → batch investigation within 7 days.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Match Analysis Agent. Analyze potential matches — fuzzy name matching, alias checking, entity resolution. Provide JSON with: potentialMatches, matchScore, analysisResult, escalationNeeded.\\"}"	\N	Match Analysis AI Agent	2.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Screening Matches\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Vendor Screening Matches\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 2 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Previously Investigated and Cleared Matches\\",\\"source\\":\\"Compliance Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Active Bookings/Payments for Matched Entities\\",\\"source\\":\\"Operations / Finance\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Actionable Match List (prioritized)\\",\\"Previously Cleared Matches (re-confirmed)\\",\\"False Positive Indicators\\",\\"Investigation Priority Queue\\",\\"Pending Transaction Freeze Recommendations\\",\\"Screening Audit Log\\"]"	"[\\"All matches triaged and prioritized\\",\\"Previously cleared matches properly documented\\",\\"Pending transactions for matched entities flagged\\",\\"Audit log captures complete screening trail\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.731993+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.731993+00
eae84ad8-4188-40fb-8320-79e2d88e1aa2	\N	E2E-27-S09	Physical delivery coordination	Coordinate physical bunker delivery between supplier, port agent, and vessel. Pre-delivery: confirm vessel ETA with agent, arrange barge (supplier responsibility but agent coordinates timing), verify manifold compatibility (vessel receiving manifold vs barge delivery hose), and conduct pre-delivery meeting (vessel chief engineer, barge master: agree on pumping rate, tank sequence, communication, and emergency procedures). MARPOL requirements: ensure oil record book is ready, scupper plugs in place, and spill response equipment available. For barge delivery: barge comes alongside, connects hose to vessel manifold, and commences pumping. Delivery duration: typically 4-12 hours depending on quantity.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	input	Port Agent / Chief Engineer	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Bunker Stem Confirmation\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 8 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:8\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel ETA and Berth/Anchorage\\",\\"source\\":\\"Operations\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Barge Schedule (from supplier)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Supplier\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel Manifold Specifications\\",\\"source\\":\\"Technical\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Delivery Coordinated\\",\\"Pre-delivery Meeting Completed\\",\\"Barge Alongside Time\\",\\"Pumping Commenced Time\\",\\"MARPOL Compliance Confirmed\\"]"	"[\\"Pre-delivery meeting documented\\",\\"Manifold compatibility confirmed\\",\\"MARPOL requirements met\\",\\"Communication plan established\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.710149+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.710149+00
1d2332df-3767-4dc9-a0f1-511d7a0107f7	\N	E2E-27-S10	Quantity survey (BDN verification)	Verify quantity delivered through independent measurement and BDN (bunker delivery note) verification. Quantity measurement: vessel tanks sounded before and after delivery (opening and closing soundings), barge tanks sounded before and after (if accessible), and flow meter readings (where installed). Compare: quantity per vessel soundings vs quantity per BDN (supplier's declared quantity). Tolerance: typically ±0.5% acceptable. If discrepancy >0.5%: protest on BDN (note the vessel's figure alongside supplier's figure). BDN is the legal document for quantity — it records: date, time, port, vessel, supplier, grade, quantity, density, temperature, and supplier certification. Retain BDN and samples for minimum 12 months (MARPOL requirement).	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	input	Chief Engineer / Independent Surveyor	2.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Opening Tank Soundings (pre-delivery)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Vessel\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Closing Tank Soundings (post-delivery)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Vessel\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"BDN from Supplier\\",\\"source\\":\\"Supplier / Barge\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Flow Meter Readings (if available)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Vessel\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Quantity per Vessel Soundings (MT)\\",\\"Quantity per BDN (MT)\\",\\"Variance (%)\\",\\"BDN Signed/Protested\\",\\"Samples Retained\\"]"	"[\\"Soundings taken per standard procedure\\",\\"Variance calculated\\",\\"BDN properly signed or protested\\",\\"Samples labeled and stored per MARPOL\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.713669+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.713669+00
7e6ecbe0-5965-4e38-9b47-dda461d215cc	\N	E2E-27-S11	Quality testing (ISO 8217)	Test fuel quality against ISO 8217 specifications. Three samples taken at delivery: one for supplier, one for vessel (MARPOL mandatory retention — sealed, labeled, stored 12 months), and one for independent laboratory testing. Lab tests: density, viscosity (at 50°C), sulphur content (critical for IMO 2020 — must be ≤0.50% for VLSFO), flash point (minimum 60°C for safety), pour point, water content, ash content, vanadium, sodium, aluminum+silicon (cat fines — abrasive particles that destroy engine components), and total sediment. Results compared against ISO 8217 limits for the specified grade. For VLSFO: compatibility testing also recommended (can this fuel safely mix with existing ROB without causing sludge?). Results available in 5-10 business days.	\N	system	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Fuel Quality Agent. Validate fuel quality against ISO 8217 specifications — viscosity, density, sulfur, water content. Provide JSON with: qualityResults, iso8217Compliant, sulfurPercent, issues.\\"}"	\N	Independent Testing Laboratory	240.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Fuel Sample\\",\\"source\\":\\"Delivery Sampling\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Specified ISO 8217 Grade\\",\\"source\\":\\"PO / Stem\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Compatibility Test Request (if VLSFO)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Technical\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Lab Test Report\\",\\"Pass/Fail per Parameter\\",\\"Sulphur Content\\",\\"Cat Fines Level (Al+Si)\\",\\"Compatibility Result (if tested)\\",\\"Overall Quality Assessment\\"]"	"[\\"All ISO 8217 parameters tested\\",\\"Sulphur ≤0.50% for VLSFO\\",\\"Cat fines within limits (<60ppm)\\",\\"Results reported against specified grade\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.716927+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.716927+00
87769b8c-f37d-404f-80a8-b549116ac967	\N	E2E-27-S12	Quality gate: accept or reject fuel	Decision on fuel quality based on lab results. If all parameters within ISO 8217 limits: accept fuel for use. If off-spec: assess severity. Critical failures (reject immediately): sulphur >0.50% (IMO violation, heavy fines), flash point <60°C (safety hazard), or extreme cat fines (>80ppm — engine damage risk). Manageable deviations: slightly elevated cat fines (40-60ppm — can use with enhanced purifier operation), marginally out-of-spec viscosity (adjust heating). For off-spec fuel: options are: 1) reject and demand replacement (supplier liability), 2) accept at discount (negotiate reduced price), or 3) debunker (pump fuel off vessel back to barge — expensive, last resort). File quality claim against supplier for any off-spec delivery.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Technical Superintendent / Bunker Manager	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Lab Test Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 11 output\\",\\"required\\":true,\\"providedBy\\":\\"step:11\\"},{\\"field\\":\\"ISO 8217 Specification Limits\\",\\"source\\":\\"Standards\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Engine Manufacturer Fuel Specifications\\",\\"source\\":\\"Technical\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Decision (accept/conditional accept/reject)\\",\\"Quality Claim Filed (Y/N)\\",\\"Mitigation Measures (if conditional accept)\\",\\"Debunkering Order (if reject)\\"]"	"[\\"All parameters reviewed against limits\\",\\"Critical failures trigger immediate reject\\",\\"Mitigation measures adequate for conditional accept\\",\\"Quality claim filed within contractual deadline\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.720738+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.720738+00
