a12b70ec-1186-4201-bb85-d03c132baa4e	\N	E2E-30-S02	Incident gate: severity assessment	Claims manager reviews the incident investigation report and classifies the severity level, which determines the claims handling pathway. Severity levels: (1) MINOR (estimated <USD 10,000) — handle in-house with standard documentation, no survey required unless disputed; (2) MODERATE (USD 10,000-100,000) — appoint independent surveyor, notify P&I Club correspondent, follow standard claims procedure; (3) MAJOR (USD 100,000-1M) — immediate P&I Club notification, appoint specialist surveyor and legal counsel, establish claims reserve, management oversight; (4) CATASTROPHIC (>USD 1M or General Average) — full crisis response team, P&I Club leads, board notification, potential General Average declaration. Decision also covers: whether to appoint surveyor (mandatory for moderate+), which surveyor firm to use (from approved panel), whether legal counsel needed, initial liability position (admit, deny, or investigate further), and whether to invoke any cargo insurance policy the company holds.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Claims Manager	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Incident Investigation Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Estimated Damage Value\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Preliminary Cause Assessment\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"P&I Club Deductible Schedule\\",\\"source\\":\\"Insurance Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Severity Classification (Minor/Moderate/Major/Catastrophic)\\",\\"Survey Decision (required/not required)\\",\\"Appointed Surveyor (if required)\\",\\"Legal Counsel Decision\\",\\"Initial Claims Reserve Amount\\",\\"P&I Club Notification Authorization\\"]"	"[\\"Severity classification matches estimated damage thresholds\\",\\"Surveyor appointed for all moderate+ claims\\",\\"Claims reserve amount set based on damage estimate plus contingency\\",\\"P&I notification triggered for claims above deductible\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.783128+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.783128+00
65e49b44-aea6-482a-9410-a5babc9b1132	\N	E2E-30-S04	Survey appointment	Appoint an independent cargo surveyor from the approved panel to inspect the damaged cargo and provide an impartial assessment. Selection criteria: (1) Surveyor must be independent (not employed by either party); (2) Qualification — IICL certified for containers, appropriate commodity expertise for cargo; (3) Geographical availability — must be able to reach the cargo location within 48 hours; (4) P&I Club approval — for large claims, the P&I Club may insist on their preferred surveyor; (5) Joint survey preference — invite the claimant's surveyor to participate for transparency. Notify claimant of survey date/time/location. The survey must happen before cargo is disposed of, repaired, or moved (this is critical — if cargo is disposed of without survey, liability becomes harder to contest). For perishable cargo, expedited survey within 24 hours. Issue formal survey appointment letter with scope of inspection.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Liability Assessment Agent. Assess liability — Hague-Visby rules, bill of lading terms, carrier defenses. Provide JSON with: liabilityBasis, carrierDefense, exposureAmount, liabilityPercent.\\"}"	input	Claims Manager	12.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Claim Record with Cargo Location\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 3 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Approved Surveyor Panel\\",\\"source\\":\\"Master Data\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"P&I Club Surveyor Requirements (if applicable)\\",\\"source\\":\\"P&I Club\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Claimant Surveyor Contact (for joint survey)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Claimant\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Surveyor Appointment Letter\\",\\"Survey Date/Time/Location\\",\\"Joint Survey Confirmation\\",\\"Survey Scope of Inspection\\",\\"Claimant Notification of Survey\\"]"	"[\\"Surveyor is independent and appropriately qualified\\",\\"Survey scheduled before any cargo disposal\\",\\"Claimant notified and invited to joint survey\\",\\"Perishable cargo survey expedited within 24 hours\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.787086+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.787086+00
9d55c162-730d-4461-8832-081931536872	\N	E2E-30-S05	Joint survey execution	Conduct the joint cargo survey at the damage location. The surveyor inspects: (1) Container external condition — dents, holes, roof damage, door seal integrity; (2) Container internal condition — cleanliness, odor, moisture, previous cargo residue; (3) Cargo damage extent — physical examination, sampling (for contamination), temperature logs (for reefer); (4) Stowage and securing adequacy — was cargo properly secured inside container; (5) Seal condition — intact, broken, or tampered; (6) Tally check — count against BL quantity to verify shortage claims; (7) Photographs — numbered and described, showing container markings, seal numbers, damage detail; (8) Sample collection — for contamination claims, collect samples for lab analysis with chain of custody. The surveyor produces a preliminary survey report on-site and a final detailed report within 7-14 days. Both parties (carrier surveyor and claimant surveyor) sign the joint survey findings.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	input	Independent Surveyor / Claims Manager	24.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Survey Appointment Details\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 4 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Container and Cargo Details\\",\\"source\\":\\"Claim Record\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Reefer Temperature Logs (if applicable)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Equipment Module\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"BL Cargo Manifest (for tally check)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Documentation Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Preliminary Survey Report (on-site)\\",\\"Photographic Evidence Package (numbered)\\",\\"Sample Collection Records (if contamination)\\",\\"Joint Survey Findings (signed by both parties)\\",\\"Estimated Sound and Damaged Values\\",\\"Surveyor's Preliminary Cause Opinion\\"]"	"[\\"Survey conducted before cargo disposal or repair\\",\\"All photos numbered and catalogued with descriptions\\",\\"Tally count documented against BL quantities\\",\\"Joint survey findings signed by all attending parties\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.790674+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.790674+00
98827487-7f7e-4194-b06c-fd092cdea4d6	\N	E2E-30-S08	Liability gate: accept or contest liability	Senior claims manager (or legal counsel for major claims) makes the liability determination based on all evidence. Decision matrix: (1) ACCEPT LIABILITY — carrier was negligent, no viable defense, settle within Hague-Visby limits; (2) PARTIAL LIABILITY — shared fault (e.g., shipper's poor packing + carrier's improper stowage), negotiate proportion; (3) CONTEST LIABILITY — strong defense exists (force majeure, inherent vice, insufficiency of packing by shipper), deny claim with supporting evidence; (4) REFER TO P&I CLUB — claim exceeds deductible or involves complex legal issues, P&I Club takes over handling. Consider: strength of evidence, legal costs of contesting vs settlement amount, relationship impact with the customer, precedent effect (accepting liability on weak evidence encourages future claims), and time bar proximity (approaching time bar may force faster decision). Document the liability rationale thoroughly as it may be needed in arbitration or court proceedings.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Senior Claims Manager / Legal Counsel	24.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Loss Prevention Analysis Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Complete Claims Docket\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 6 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Hague-Visby Defense Assessment\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Legal Advice (for major claims)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Legal Department\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Customer Relationship Value\\",\\"source\\":\\"CRM Module\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Liability Decision (Accept/Partial/Contest/Refer to P&I)\\",\\"Liability Rationale Document\\",\\"Settlement Authority Amount (if accepting)\\",\\"Defense Brief (if contesting)\\",\\"P&I Club Referral (if applicable)\\"]"	"[\\"Liability decision supported by evidence and legal analysis\\",\\"Settlement authority within DOA matrix for claims\\",\\"Defense brief references specific Hague-Visby provisions\\",\\"Time bar deadline considered in decision timing\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.795791+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.795791+00
336f5615-63dc-4282-b55f-3fa2ee5d0e72	\N	E2E-30-S11	Negotiation with claimant/P&I	Conduct claim settlement negotiations with the claimant (or their insurer/lawyer) and coordinate with P&I Club. Negotiation considerations: (1) Starting position — based on liability decision (full admit, partial, or deny); (2) Hague-Visby limitation — carrier can limit liability to 2 SDR/kg or 666.67 SDR/package (whichever is higher), unless claimant can prove willful misconduct; (3) Quantum assessment — agreed damaged value vs sound value, salvage value of damaged cargo, mitigation efforts by consignee; (4) Counter-offers and concessions — track each round of negotiation with amounts; (5) Without prejudice discussions — all negotiation communications marked 'without prejudice' to protect position if litigation follows; (6) Time pressure — if time bar is approaching, urgency increases; (7) Multi-party negotiations — may involve carrier, claimant, shipper, terminal operator, and their respective insurers; (8) Alternative dispute resolution — consider mediation if direct negotiation stalls. Record every negotiation communication (calls, emails, meetings) in the claims docket.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	\N	input	Claims Manager / P&I Club Correspondent	120.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Liability Decision and Authority Amount\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 8 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"P&I Club Instructions\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 10 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Hague-Visby Limitation Calculation\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 3 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Claimant's Demand and Supporting Documents\\",\\"source\\":\\"Claimant\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Negotiation Log (all rounds)\\",\\"Current Offer/Counter-Offer Position\\",\\"Agreed Settlement Amount (if reached)\\",\\"Without Prejudice Correspondence File\\",\\"Mediation Referral (if applicable)\\"]"	"[\\"All communications marked 'without prejudice'\\",\\"Settlement authority not exceeded without escalation\\",\\"P&I Club informed of all material developments\\",\\"Time bar deadline monitored throughout negotiations\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.800361+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.800361+00
cb986cc8-a420-4147-9515-66b8aaa893ae	\N	E2E-30-S12	Settlement gate: approve amount	Final approval of the negotiated settlement amount per the Delegation of Authority (DOA) matrix. Approval levels: (1) Claims Manager — up to USD 25,000; (2) Claims Director — USD 25,001 - 100,000; (3) CFO — USD 100,001 - 500,000; (4) CEO — USD 500,001 - 1,000,000; (5) Board — >USD 1,000,000. Settlement documentation must include: settlement amount breakdown, payment terms (lump sum, installments), release and discharge agreement (claimant waives further claims), contribution from P&I Club (net cost to company), and any conditions (e.g., claimant returns undamaged portion of cargo). If settlement is above claims reserve, approve the reserve adjustment. Both parties must sign the settlement agreement before payment is processed.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	\N	approval	Approver per DOA Matrix	24.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Negotiated Settlement Amount\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 11 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Settlement Terms and Conditions\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 11 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"P&I Club Contribution Amount\\",\\"source\\":\\"P&I Club\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Net Cost to Company (after insurance)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Calculated\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Current Claims Reserve\\",\\"source\\":\\"Finance Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Settlement Approval (Approved/Rejected/Escalated)\\",\\"Signed Settlement Agreement\\",\\"Release and Discharge Document\\",\\"Reserve Adjustment (if needed)\\",\\"Payment Authorization\\"]"	"[\\"Approval obtained at correct DOA level\\",\\"Settlement agreement includes full release and discharge\\",\\"Reserve adjusted to match settlement amount\\",\\"Payment terms clearly documented\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.803781+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.803781+00
53347dff-dc58-4b49-9fc5-da30e68669c1	\N	E2E-30-S17	GA gate: approve GA declaration	Board-level approval for General Average declaration. GA is an extraordinary event that affects every customer with cargo on the vessel and can result in significant reputational and operational impact. The board (or CEO with board delegated authority) must approve: (1) GA declaration is legally justified under York-Antwerp Rules; (2) Selected GA adjuster firm is appropriate; (3) Communication strategy to affected customers and agents; (4) Cash flow impact — GA bonds/deposits may be required from our own cargo (if we have own cargo aboard); (5) Legal counsel confirmation that GA conditions are properly met; (6) Media/PR strategy if the incident has public visibility. The board may also review the overall crisis response and authorize additional resources for managing the GA process.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	\N	approval	Board / CEO	12.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"GA Declaration Package\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 16 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Legal Counsel Opinion on GA Validity\\",\\"source\\":\\"Legal Department\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Number of Affected Customers/BLs\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 16 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Estimated Cash Flow Impact\\",\\"source\\":\\"Finance Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"GA Declaration Approval\\",\\"Communication Strategy Approval\\",\\"Board Resolution Document\\",\\"Authority to Proceed with GA Process\\"]"	"[\\"Legal opinion confirms GA conditions met\\",\\"Board resolution signed and recorded\\",\\"Communication plan covers all affected stakeholders\\",\\"Financial impact assessed and approved\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.809512+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.809512+00
