9ba53dca-d261-4d53-8d23-da0ed02965fd	\N	E2E-31-S07	CII gate: review D/E rated vessels, approve corrective plan	Fleet operations director reviews all D and E rated vessels from the CII calculation and approves corrective action plans. Per IMO regulations, D-rated vessels must develop a corrective action plan within 3 years and E-rated vessels must develop one immediately. The corrective plan must be included in the Ship Energy Efficiency Management Plan (SEEMP Part III). Review includes: (1) Root cause analysis — why is the vessel rated D/E (speed profile, route inefficiency, hull condition, engine performance, age/design); (2) Technical measures — hull cleaning, propeller polishing, energy-saving devices (bulbous bow retrofit, Mewis duct, rotor sails); (3) Operational measures — speed optimization, weather routing, trim optimization, port turnaround reduction; (4) Commercial measures — route redeployment to shorter routes, cargo optimization for better utilization, consider vessel sale/scrap if CII improvement is not economically viable; (5) Financial impact — cost of corrective measures vs penalty of continued D/E rating (future commercial disadvantage as charterers increasingly demand CII A/B vessels).	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a MARPOL Summary Agent. Generate MARPOL compliance summary for the reporting period. Provide JSON with: annexCompliance, violations, correctiveActions, overallStatus.\\"}"	decision	Fleet Operations Director	24.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"D/E Rated Vessel List with Root Causes\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 3 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Improvement Scenario Models\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 3 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel Technical Condition Reports\\",\\"source\\":\\"Technical Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Corrective Measure Cost Estimates\\",\\"source\\":\\"Finance Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Approved Corrective Action Plan per D/E Vessel\\",\\"SEEMP Part III Updates\\",\\"Investment Approval for Technical Measures\\",\\"Vessel Redeployment Decisions\\",\\"Vessel Disposal Recommendations (if applicable)\\",\\"CII Improvement Targets and Timeline\\"]"	"[\\"Every D/E vessel has an approved corrective plan\\",\\"SEEMP Part III updated per IMO requirements\\",\\"Budget approved for technical measures\\",\\"Timeline ensures compliance within IMO deadlines (3 years for D, immediate for E)\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.820947+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.820947+00
dd3cc4ec-1e9e-4a81-a8ad-f335a4856151	\N	E2E-31-S12	EU ETS allowance calculation	Calculate EU Emissions Trading System (EU ETS) allowance requirements for maritime shipping. EU ETS applies to vessels ≥5,000 GT from 2024 with phase-in: 40% of emissions in 2024, 70% in 2025, 100% from 2026. Coverage: 100% of intra-EU voyages, 50% of extra-EU voyages (EU port to/from non-EU port), and 100% of emissions at berth in EU ports. Calculate: (1) Total CO2 emissions within EU ETS scope (using EU MRV data); (2) Apply phase-in percentage for current year; (3) Determine EUA (EU Allowance) requirement — 1 EUA per tonne CO2; (4) Assess current EUA holdings vs requirement — do we need to purchase additional allowances; (5) EUA price forecast and budget impact (EUAs were ~€80-100/tonne in 2024-2025); (6) Compliance deadline — surrender allowances by 30 September for prior year emissions. Consider: (a) Free allocation — shipping receives no free allocation (100% auctioning); (b) Alternative compliance — if using alternative fuels with zero/low emissions, fewer allowances needed; (c) Trading strategy — should we buy EUAs now (forward contracts) or wait (price speculation).	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	\N	EU ETS Compliance AI Agent	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"EU MRV Emission Data (EU-scope voyages)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 11 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"EU ETS Phase-In Percentage (current year)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Regulatory Reference\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Current EUA Holdings\\",\\"source\\":\\"Treasury Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"EUA Market Price (spot and forward)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Carbon Market Data\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Alternative Fuel Emission Reductions\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 8 Output\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"EU ETS Allowance Requirement (tonnes)\\",\\"Phase-In Adjusted Requirement\\",\\"EUA Shortfall/Surplus\\",\\"Budget Impact (EUA purchase cost)\\",\\"Surrender Deadline Tracker\\",\\"EUA Trading Strategy Recommendation\\"]"	"[\\"EU ETS scope correctly applied (intra/extra/berth split)\\",\\"Phase-in percentage matches current year regulation\\",\\"EUA calculation reconciles with EU MRV emission data\\",\\"Surrender deadline (30 September) tracked per vessel\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.827495+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.827495+00
ebc2523c-c96f-4e5e-9c54-1af3e36944d6	\N	E2E-31-S17	ESG gate: management review before publication	CEO/Board ESG committee reviews the draft sustainability report before publication. Review focuses on: (1) Accuracy — are all numbers correct and reconciled with financial reporting; (2) Completeness — are all material topics covered per stakeholder expectations; (3) Forward-looking statements — are targets and commitments achievable and accurately stated; (4) Legal review — no inadvertent admissions or statements that create liability; (5) Regulatory compliance — meets disclosure requirements in all jurisdictions (EU CSRD if applicable, SEC climate disclosure if US-listed); (6) Competitor positioning — how do our metrics compare with published peer reports; (7) Stakeholder communications — press release, investor presentation, website updates. Approve for publication or return with specific amendments. Consider timing of publication relative to annual report, AGM, and investor events.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	\N	approval	CEO / Board ESG Committee	72.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Draft Sustainability Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 16 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Legal Review Comments\\",\\"source\\":\\"Legal Department\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Peer Comparison Analysis\\",\\"source\\":\\"ESG Module\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"EU CSRD Requirements (if applicable)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Compliance Module\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Publication Approval (Approved/Amend)\\",\\"Amendments Required (if any)\\",\\"Approved Final Report\\",\\"Communication Plan (press, investors, website)\\",\\"Publication Date\\"]"	"[\\"All numbers reconciled with audited financial data\\",\\"Legal review completed with no unresolved concerns\\",\\"Forward-looking statements include appropriate caveats\\",\\"Publication timing coordinated with investor calendar\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.837484+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.837484+00
08e9154e-2a1f-4480-9c00-635ffaf70963	\N	E2E-31-S18	Third-party audit coordination	Coordinate the third-party assurance/audit of the sustainability report to enhance credibility. Assurance levels: (1) Limited assurance — procedures are less extensive, conclusion stated in negative form ('nothing has come to our attention...'), lower cost, suitable for first-time reporters; (2) Reasonable assurance — more extensive procedures, positive-form conclusion ('in our opinion, the report presents fairly...'), higher credibility, required by some frameworks (EU CSRD mandates limited moving to reasonable). Select assurance provider: Big 4 accounting firm, specialist sustainability assurance firm, or classification society (for vessel-specific data). Scope of assurance: typically covers Scope 1/2 emissions and selected KPIs (not always full Scope 3). Process: (1) Agree scope and standards (ISAE 3000, AA1000AS); (2) Provide supporting data and documentation; (3) Facilitate site visits and interviews; (4) Review draft assurance statement; (5) Publish assurance statement alongside sustainability report. Timeline: typically 4-6 weeks from report draft to assurance statement.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	\N	input	Head of ESG / Finance Director	240.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Approved Sustainability Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 17 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Supporting Data and Evidence Package\\",\\"source\\":\\"All Prior Steps\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Assurance Provider Engagement\\",\\"source\\":\\"Procurement Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Prior Year Assurance Statement\\",\\"source\\":\\"ESG Module\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Assurance Statement from Third Party\\",\\"Management Letter (findings and recommendations)\\",\\"Assurance Scope and Level Achieved\\",\\"Data Corrections (if any identified during audit)\\",\\"Final Published Sustainability Report (with assurance)\\"]"	"[\\"Assurance conducted per ISAE 3000 or equivalent standard\\",\\"Scope covers at minimum Scope 1 and 2 emissions\\",\\"Management letter findings addressed before publication\\",\\"Assurance statement published alongside sustainability report\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.84208+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.84208+00
