0e4e78ae-d38d-4cd3-8838-79d893b795d5	\N	E2E-32-S02	Emergency gate: confirm situation and authorize response	DPA/Operations Director confirms the emergency classification and authorizes the response level and budget. Decisions: (1) Confirm or reclassify emergency level based on latest information; (2) Authorize resources — salvage engagement (LOF/SCOPIC terms), tug mobilization, emergency drydock, helicopter medevac, spill response vessels; (3) Budget authorization — Level 2/3 emergencies can cost millions; authorize initial response budget with escalation thresholds; (4) Media/communications strategy — appoint spokesperson, prepare holding statement, activate social media monitoring; (5) Legal engagement — appoint maritime lawyers (for salvage, GA, regulatory defense); (6) Crew welfare — arrange family notification if crew injuries, appoint crew welfare coordinator. For Level 3 (full crisis): activate the Crisis Management Team (CMT), which includes CEO, CFO, legal counsel, and communications director in addition to SERT.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	DPA / Operations Director	1.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Initial SITREP\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Emergency Level Classification\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Resource Requirements Assessment\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Insurance Policy Coverage Summary\\",\\"source\\":\\"Insurance Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Confirmed Emergency Level\\",\\"Response Authorization (resources and budget)\\",\\"Crisis Team Activation (if Level 3)\\",\\"Media Strategy Decision\\",\\"Legal Counsel Engagement\\",\\"Crew Welfare Arrangements\\"]"	"[\\"Emergency level confirmed with documented rationale\\",\\"Budget authorization matches expected response costs\\",\\"Legal counsel engaged for maritime emergencies\\",\\"Crew welfare arrangements initiated for any 