0d72d0c0-7ae3-4585-b6f4-95ac2fc5b828	\N	E2E-32-S08	GA gate: declare GA?	Board/CEO makes the decision whether to declare General Average based on the assessment. This is a major commercial decision affecting all customers on the vessel. Considerations: (1) Legal basis — is the GA assessment legally sound (will it withstand challenge from cargo interests or their insurers); (2) Commercial impact — GA declaration affects customer relationships, particularly for major accounts; cargo interests must post security before collecting their cargo; (3) Reputational risk — GA declaration is a public event that attracts media attention; (4) Alternative approaches — could the costs be absorbed without GA (if relatively small compared to total contributing values, the administrative cost of GA adjustment may not be justified); (5) Insurance coverage — P&I Club and H&M policies cover the company's own GA contribution; (6) GA adjuster recommendation — if a GA adjuster has been consulted, consider their professional opinion. Decide: DECLARE GA (proceed to formal declaration), or ABSORB COSTS (waive GA and absorb extraordinary costs, claiming from own insurers only).	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Board / CEO	12.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"GA Assessment Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Legal Counsel Opinion on GA Validity\\",\\"source\\":\\"Legal Department\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Number of Affected Customers\\",\\"source\\":\\"Manifest Data\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"P&I Club Recommendation\\",\\"source\\":\\"P&I Club\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"GA Decision (Declare/Absorb)\\",\\"Board Resolution (if declaring)\\",\\"Legal Authorization\\",\\"Communication Strategy\\"]"	"[\\"Decision documented with rationale\\",\\"Legal counsel confirms GA conditions met (if declaring)\\",\\"P&I Club position considered\\",\\"Communication strategy approved before declaration\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.858814+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.858814+00
ab68a828-5f1f-4338-8cf2-ca0ab592f8d4	\N	E2E-32-S10	Cargo interest notifications	Notify all cargo interests (BL holders) of the General Average declaration and their obligation to provide security before collecting their cargo. Each BL holder receives: (1) GA declaration notice with reference to applicable York-Antwerp Rules; (2) GA bond form — to be completed and returned with cargo insurer's guarantee; (3) Estimated contributory value of their cargo (CIF value); (4) Estimated GA contribution percentage (preliminary, final amount determined by adjuster); (5) Instructions for providing security — cash deposit to GA adjuster's account or guarantee from cargo insurer; (6) Contact details for GA adjuster for queries; (7) Warning that cargo will not be released without adequate security. For consignees without cargo insurance: they must provide cash deposit equal to their estimated contribution (this can cause significant problems for uninsured cargo). Notify destination port agents to withhold delivery until GA security is received. Track security collection progress — for large container vessels this involves thousands of BLs across dozens of ports.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	\N	Cargo Notification AI Agent	12.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"GA Declaration Details\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 9 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Full Manifest with All BL Holders\\",\\"source\\":\\"Documentation Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"GA Security Requirements per BL\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 9 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Destination Port Agent Contacts\\",\\"source\\":\\"Port Agency Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"GA Bond Forms and Instructions\\",\\"source\\":\\"GA Adjuster\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"BL-Level GA Notifications Sent\\",\\"GA Bond Forms Distributed\\",\\"Port Agent Instructions (hold cargo)\\",\\"Security Collection Tracking Dashboard\\",\\"Uninsured Cargo Owner Alerts\\",\\"Customer Query Contact Routing\\"]"	"[\\"Every BL holder notified with correct contributory value\\",\\"Port agents instructed at all discharge ports\\",\\"Security tracking dashboard operational\\",\\"Customer inquiry routing established\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.864255+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.864255+00
6b7712e8-f4be-458c-b7d6-e923edf9f4a8	\N	E2E-32-S15	Post-incident gate: approve corrective actions	Safety committee / board reviews the investigation findings and approves corrective actions to prevent recurrence. This is the ISM Code 'continual improvement' step. Review: (1) Root cause from investigation — approve or challenge the root cause analysis; (2) Corrective actions — specific, measurable, assigned, time-bound actions to address each contributing factor. Examples: install additional safety equipment, modify SMS procedures, enhance training programs, change watchkeeping arrangements, modify route planning criteria, upgrade equipment, improve maintenance schedules; (3) Fleet-wide applicability — determine which corrective actions apply to all vessels vs only the affected vessel; (4) Budget approval — corrective actions may require capital expenditure (equipment upgrades) or operational changes (additional crew, slower speeds); (5) Verification plan — how and when will the effectiveness of corrective actions be verified (follow-up audit, specific testing, drill scenario); (6) ISM Code compliance — update the Safety Management System (SMS) documentation to reflect changes; notify classification society of SMS amendments. Share lessons learned with fleet through safety bulletin.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	\N	approval	Safety Committee / Board	72.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Investigation Report with Root Cause\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 6 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Corrective Action Recommendations\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 6 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Risk Register Update\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 13 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Budget Impact of Corrective Actions\\",\\"source\\":\\"Finance Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Fleet-Wide Applicability Assessment\\",\\"source\\":\\"Technical Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Approved Corrective Actions Plan\\",\\"Budget Authorization per Action\\",\\"Fleet-Wide Implementation Plan\\",\\"SMS Update Requirements\\",\\"Verification Schedule\\",\\"Lessons Learned Safety Bulletin\\"]"	"[\\"Every root cause has at least one corrective action\\",\\"Budget approved for all corrective actions\\",\\"Fleet-wide implementation plan has assigned owners and deadlines\\",\\"SMS documentation updated per ISM Code requirements\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.870503+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.870503+00
