7b1db4d7-9f9a-44f2-85b5-5a379c59f2f4	\N	E2E-34-S04	Slot gate: approve slot purchase/sale plan	Commercial director reviews and approves the slot allocation plan, including any ad-hoc slot purchases or sales. Decisions: (1) Base allocation — confirm the standard allocation meets commercial demand forecast; (2) Excess slots — if demand exceeds allocation, approve purchase of additional slots from partners (at agreed slot cost or market rate); (3) Surplus slots — if demand is below allocation, decide whether to sell surplus to partners (reducing cost) or hold for potential late bookings; (4) Strategic slots — reserve capacity for high-yield cargo even if overall utilization is below target; (5) MQC compliance — ensure we can meet minimum quantity commitments to avoid penalties; (6) Seasonal adjustments — approve increased allocation for peak season and reduced allocation for off-peak. Financial impact: slot purchases increase costs, slot sales reduce costs but may leave us short if demand surges. Balance commercial optimization against partnership commitments.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Commercial Director	12.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Slot Allocation Plan\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 3 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Demand Forecast vs Allocation Gap Analysis\\",\\"source\\":\\"Commercial Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Slot Purchase/Sale Price Schedule\\",\\"source\\":\\"Alliance Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"MQC Compliance Status\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 3 Output\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Approved Slot Plan\\",\\"Slot Purchase Orders (if needed)\\",\\"Slot Sale Offers (if surplus)\\",\\"Seasonal Adjustment Approvals\\",\\"Budget Impact of Slot Transactions\\"]"	"[\\"Slot plan supports commercial demand targets\\",\\"Purchase/sale decisions within budget authority\\",\\"MQC compliance ensured for the period\\",\\"Seasonal adjustments coordinated with partners\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	202