115ff9a7-0e4d-4667-8bd5-290b9013d521	\N	E2E-34-S15	Performance gate: continue/modify/exit VSA	Executive committee reviews VSA performance and decides the strategic direction. Options: (1) CONTINUE — VSA is performing well, renew or extend; (2) MODIFY — VSA is performing adequately but adjustments needed (change slot allocation, modify cost-sharing formula, add/remove ports from rotation, adjust vessel size); (3) EXIT — VSA is underperforming, issue termination notice per agreement terms (typically 6-12 months notice). Decision factors: (a) Financial performance — is the VSA margin above company hurdle rate; (b) Strategic fit — does the VSA serve markets that align with company strategy; (c) Partner quality — are partners reliable (schedule, equipment, safety, financial stability); (d) Market conditions — has the market changed since VSA was signed (demand shifts, new competitors, regulatory changes); (e) Alternative options — could we do better with a different partner, different route, or own-vessel deployment. If modifying: negotiate amendments with partners. If exiting: plan transition (redeploy own vessels, find alternative partner, or withdraw from trade lane).	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	decision	Executive Committee	48.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"VSA Performance Dashboard\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 14 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Market Intelligence (trade lane outlook)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Analytics Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Alternative Deployment Options\\",\\"source\\":\\"Fleet Planning Module\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Partner Relationship Assessment\\",\\"source\\":\\"Alliance Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"VSA Strategy Decision (Continue/Modify/Exit)\\",\\"Modification Requirements (if modify)\\",\\"Termination Notice (if exit)\\",\\"Transition Plan (if exit)\\",\\"Negotiation Mandate (if modify)\\"]"	"[\\"Decision documented with financial and strategic rationale\\",