ab8cd93a-9847-4075-a590-5b1e4ad553cc	\N	E2E-38-S03	Cert gate: verify all certificates valid	Crew superintendent manually verifies the AI-generated certificate report and confirms all joining crew meet documentary requirements. Physical verification of original documents: (1) Confirm certificate authenticity — cross-reference with issuing authority databases where available (e.g., IMO GISIS STCW module); (2) Check for alterations or inconsistencies; (3) Verify photographs match the crew member; (4) Confirm flag state endorsement is genuine (some endorsements can be verified online with flag state registries); (5) Ensure special qualifications match the assigned position (e.g., chief engineer has correct engine power rating on CoC). If any certificate is invalid, expired, or unverifiable: (a) Source replacement crew with valid certificates; (b) Arrange emergency certificate renewal if possible (some flag states offer express processing); (c) Delay crew change if no alternative. This gate is critical — putting uncertified crew on board exposes the company to PSC detention, ISM non-conformities, and P&I Club liability exclusions.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Crew Superintendent	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Certificate Validity Report\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 2 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Original Certificate Copies/Scans\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Flag State Verification Portal Access\\",\\"source\\":\\"Flag State Authority\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Certificate Verification Decision (Pass/Fail)\\",\\"Verified Crew List (approved for joining)\\",\\"Certificate Issues (if any)\\",\\"Replacement Crew Request (if needed)\\"]"	"[\\"Each certificate verified against official database or original\\",\\"Flag state endorsement confirmed genuine\\",\\"All special qualifications match position requirements\\",\\"No crew member with expired or invalid certificates approved\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.990216+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.990216+00
2204ba1e-8464-4e94-bc3a-be936a0b2ef4	\N	E2E-38-S06	Travel booking (flights, accommodation)	Book travel arrangements for joining crew from their home location to the crew change port. Optimize: (1) Flights — book economy class per company policy (business class for senior officers on long-haul if policy permits), prefer direct flights to minimize transit risks, ensure arrival at least 12-24 hours before vessel's planned departure to allow for delays; (2) Accommodation — hotel near the port for overnight stay if arrival is day before vessel; (3) Local transport — airport to hotel and hotel to port transfers; (4) Travel insurance — confirm company travel insurance covers the crew; (5) Group bookings — if multiple crew joining at same port, coordinate group travel for cost savings. Budget considerations: compare flight costs across different airports (some crew change ports have cheaper alternatives nearby), consider seasonal pricing, and apply corporate rates where available. Generate itinerary with all confirmation numbers and share with crew, vessel master, and port agent. Include contingency plan if flights are delayed or cancelled.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Travel Booking Agent. Book travel for joining and departing crew — flights, accommodation, transfers. Provide JSON with: flightsBooked, hotelBooked, transferArranged, totalCost.\\"}"	\N	Travel Booking AI Agent	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Joining Crew Home Locations\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Crew Change Port and Date\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 1 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Visa/Transit Approvals\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 5 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Company Travel Policy\\",\\"source\\":\\"HR Policy\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Corporate Rate Agreements (airlines, hotels)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Procurement Module\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Flight Bookings (confirmation numbers)\\",\\"Hotel Reservations\\",\\"Transfer Arrangements\\",\\"Complete Itinerary per Crew Member\\",\\"Travel Cost Breakdown\\",\\"Contingency Travel Plan\\"]"	"[\\"Arrival time allows 12-24 hour buffer before vessel departure\\",\\"Travel bookings match visa-approved routing\\",\\"All crew have confirmed tickets and accommodation\\",\\"Total travel cost within approved budget\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.994557+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.994557+00
5f795f4f-6434-4da8-bcd8-1218d85b4547	\N	E2E-38-S07	Medical examination & drug/alcohol screening	Conduct pre-embarkation medical examination and drug/alcohol screening per STCW and company policy. Medical examination per ILO/WHO Guidelines for Medical Examinations of Seafarers includes: (1) Physical examination — cardiovascular, respiratory, musculoskeletal, neurological; (2) Vision test — color vision (Ishihara plates), visual acuity (standards vary by position: lookouts need 6/6, others 6/9); (3) Hearing test — audiometry for deck officers and ratings; (4) Blood tests — basic blood panel, blood sugar, cholesterol; (5) Urine analysis — drug screening (5-panel minimum: cannabis, cocaine, opiates, amphetamines, benzodiazepines) and alcohol (random breath test); (6) Chest X-ray (if required by flag state or endemic TB area); (7) Mental health assessment (if concerns flagged). Medical must be conducted by approved maritime medical examiner. Certificate valid for 2 years (1 year for under-18 crew). Zero-tolerance drug policy — any positive result is immediate disqualification.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Medical Clearance Agent. Process medical examination and drug/alcohol screening for joining crew. Provide JSON with: medicalExam, drugTest, fitForDuty, restrictions.\\"}"	input	Maritime Medical Examiner	24.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Joining Crew Medical History\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"STCW Medical Standards per Rank\\",\\"source\\":\\"Regulatory Reference\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Company Drug & Alcohol Policy\\",\\"source\\":\\"HR Policy\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Approved Maritime Medical Examiner\\",\\"source\\":\\"Medical Service Provider\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Medical Examination Results per Crew\\",\\"Drug/Alcohol Screening Results\\",\\"Medical Fitness Certificate (if passed)\\",\\"Disqualification Notice (if failed)\\",\\"Restrictions/Limitations (if conditional pass)\\",\\"Medical Certificate Validity Period\\"]"	"[\\"Medical examination conducted by approved maritime examiner\\",\\"Vision standards meet STCW requirements for assigned position\\",\\"Drug screening covers minimum 5-panel substances\\",\\"Medical certificate issued in approved format with correct validity\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:40.998275+00	2026-04-01 12:32:40.998275+00
93c9f32f-ee29-4b3a-878f-e5959f93375f	\N	E2E-38-S08	Medical gate: clear for duty	Crew superintendent reviews medical examination results and clears crew for duty. Review: (1) Medical fitness certificate — confirm it meets STCW and flag state requirements; (2) Drug/alcohol screening — zero tolerance, any positive result means immediate disqualification and replacement crew must be sourced; (3) Conditional fitness — some crew may be passed fit with restrictions (e.g., 'fit for duty, must wear corrective lenses at all times') — assess if restrictions are acceptable for the assigned position; (4) Chronic conditions — review any ongoing medical conditions and ensure they don't pose a risk at sea (diabetes controlled by medication is generally acceptable; insulin-dependent diabetes may not be); (5) Mental health — if any concerns flagged during assessment, evaluate fitness for the isolated sea environment. Clear crew for travel or arrange replacement for disqualified crew. Medical records are confidential and stored separately from general crew files.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"gate\\"}"	approval	Crew Superintendent	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Medical Examination Results\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Drug/Alcohol Screening Results\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 7 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Company Medical Fitness Policy\\",\\"source\\":\\"HR Policy\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Flag State Medical Requirements\\",\\"source\\":\\"Flag State Regulations\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Medical Clearance Decision (Clear/Disqualified/Conditional)\\",\\"Cleared Crew List\\",\\"Disqualified Crew with Replacement Request\\",\\"Conditional Restrictions Noted\\",\\"Medical Records Filed (confidential)\\"]"	"[\\"All cleared crew have valid medical fitness certificates\\",\\"Zero positive drug/alcohol results among cleared crew\\",\\"Conditional restrictions are compatible with assigned duties\\"