f1cf385c-a4e9-439a-aea8-31e3a9e2ab91	\N	E2E-38-S10	Duty handover & vessel familiarization	Departing crew members hand over duties to their replacements and conduct vessel familiarization. Per SOLAS and ISM Code requirements: (1) Position-specific handover — engine room status, deck cargo status, navigation equipment status, ongoing maintenance issues, standing orders; (2) Safety familiarization — location and operation of: life-saving appliances (lifeboats, life rafts, EPIRBs), fire-fighting equipment (CO2, foam, water mist systems), emergency procedures (fire, abandon ship, man overboard, pollution), alarm signals, muster stations; (3) Security familiarization — ISPS Code requirements, security levels, restricted areas; (4) Environmental familiarization — MARPOL procedures, garbage management plan, ballast water management; (5) Bridge/engine room familiarization — specific equipment operation, alarm systems, automation; (6) Emergency drill participation — joining crew must participate in emergency drill within 24 hours (or before departure if time permits). Handover notes should be documented and signed by both parties.	\N	human	gate	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Handover Agent. Manage duty handover — department-wise handover notes, vessel familiarization. Provide JSON with: handoverNotes, familiarizationComplete, safetyBriefing, watchSchedule.\\"}"	input	Departing/Joining Crew / Chief Officer	12.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Departing Crew Handover Notes\\",\\"source\\":\\"Vessel Operations\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel Safety Equipment Guide\\",\\"source\\":\\"Safety Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"ISM Code Vessel Procedures Manual\\",\\"source\\":\\"Safety Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Vessel-Specific Equipment Operation Guides\\",\\"source\\":\\"Technical Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Signed Handover Notes per Position\\",\\"Safety Familiarization