1c927e82-b56f-4b22-8ff2-11a63e03daa9	\N	E2E-38-S14	Allotment setup for new crew	Set up wage allotments for joining crew per their instructions. Seafarers typically allocate a portion of their monthly wages to be paid directly to family members or other beneficiaries at home. Process: (1) Collect allotment instructions — beneficiary name, relationship, bank account details, amount or percentage of wages; (2) Verify bank details — SWIFT code, IBAN, account number; (3) Set up standing allotment in payroll system; (4) Currency conversion — wages are in USD but allotments may be in beneficiary's local currency (INR for Indian crew, PHP for Filipino crew); apply company FX rate policy; (5) Allotment timing — typically monthly, aligned with payroll cycle; (6) Confirm with crew member that allotment details are correct. MLC 2006 Regulation 2.2 requires that seafarers have the right to allot their wages to families, and the employer must transmit allotments promptly and at reasonable cost.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are an Allotment Agent. Set up wage allotments for new crew — home remittance, savings. Provide JSON with: allotments, homeRemittance, savingsAllotment, netOnboard.\\"}"	\N	Payroll AI Agent	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Joining Crew Allotment Instructions\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew / HR\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Beneficiary Bank Details\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Member\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Company FX Rate Policy\\",\\"source\\":\\"Treasury Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"MLC Allotment Requirements\\",\\"source\\":\\"Regulatory Reference\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Allotment Setup Records per Crew Member\\",\\"Beneficiary Bank Verification\\",\\"Allotment Schedule (monthly amounts)\\",\\"Currency Conversion Parameters\\",\\"Crew Confirmation of Allotment Details\\"]"	"[\\"All allotment instructions collected and recorded\\",\\"Bank details verified for each beneficiary\\",\\"Allotment amounts do not exceed net wages\\",\\"MLC right to allotment properly implemented\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:41.014142+00	2026-04-01 12:32:41.014142+00
1cd3639a-b758-4d84-a5f5-661f6df74669	\N	E2E-38-S15	Crew list update	Update the official crew list reflecting the completed crew change. The crew list is a mandatory document under SOLAS and must be current at all times. Update: (1) Remove departed crew with sign-off date and discharge port; (2) Add joined crew with sign-on date, position, certificate numbers, nationality, date of birth; (3) Generate updated crew list in IMO FAL Form 5 format; (4) Submit to vessel for posting (must be displayed in a conspicuous place); (5) Update the company's central crew management system; (6) Generate updated minimum safe manning verification — confirm vessel meets flag state safe manning requirements with new crew composition; (7) Notify the company's Designated Person Ashore (DPA) of crew change completion; (8) Update the ISM Code shipboard records. The crew list must be available for inspection by port state control officers, flag state inspectors, and other authorized officials at any time.	\N	system	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Crew List Agent. Update official crew list and submit to authorities. Provide JSON with: crewListUpdated, totalCrew, flagStateNotified, submissionRef.\\"}"	\N	Crew Management System	2.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Sign-On/Sign-Off Records\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 9 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Joined Crew Full Details\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Flag State Safe Manning Requirements\\",\\"source\\":\\"Vessel Module\\",\\"required\\":true}]"	"[\\"Updated Crew List (FAL Form 5)\\",\\"Safe Manning Verification\\",\\"DPA Notification\\",\\"Central System Updated\\",\\"ISM Records Updated\\"]"	"[\\"Crew list reflects actual crew on board\\",\\"Safe manning requirements met with current crew\\",\\"FAL Form 5 format correct and complete\\",\\"DPA notified within 24 hours of crew change\\"]"	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-01 12:32:41.017439+00	2026-04