aa945b28-b86f-473f-b4e9-884c4a21fd9a	\N	E2E-38-S17	Departing crew repatriation	Arrange repatriation travel for departing crew from the crew change port back to their home location. MLC 2006 Regulation 2.5 requires the shipowner to bear the cost of repatriation. Arrangements: (1) Flights — book return flights to crew member's home port/city as specified in their SEA; (2) Transit visas — if routing requires transit through third countries, arrange transit visas; (3) Accommodation — if departure flight is not same day as sign-off, arrange hotel and meals; (4) Local transport — port to airport transfers; (5) Personal effects — ensure all crew personal belongings are collected from vessel; (6) Travel documents — ensure crew has all documents needed for transit and entry to home country; (7) Health requirements — some countries require health declarations for returning travelers. Track crew until they reach home — company has duty of care until repatriation is complete. Special cases: if crew is sick or injured, arrange medical repatriation (medevac if severe) with medical escort if needed.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Repatriation Agent. Arrange departing crew repatriation — travel, documentation, customs. Provide JSON with: repatriationRoute, flightsBooked, documentation, estimatedCost.\\"}"	\N	Repatriation Travel AI Agent	8.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Departing Crew Details and Home Addresses\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Sign-Off Date and Crew Change Port\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 9 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"SEA Repatriation Terms\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Transit Visa Requirements\\",\\"source\\":\\"Immigration Reference\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Medical Status (if sick/injured crew)\\",\\"source\\":\\"Medical Module\\",\\"required\\":false}]"	"[\\"Return Flight Bookings\\"