3a965feb-8ec5-403a-b943-3d97e13d635f	\N	E2E-38-S18	Leave pay calculation for departing crew	Calculate and process final leave pay entitlement for departing crew. MLC 2006 Regulation 2.4 provides for minimum 2.5 calendar days of annual leave per month of service. Calculate: (1) Leave entitlement — per SEA/CBA terms (typically 8-12 days per month of service depending on rank and CBA); (2) Leave earned during this contract — sign-on to sign-off period; (3) Leave already taken (if any shore leave was granted during contract); (4) Carried forward balance (from previous contracts, if company policy permits); (5) Leave pay rate — basic wage plus fixed allowances per CBA; (6) Payment method — some CBAs require leave pay to be paid in advance, others upon completion of leave; (7) Pro-rata calculation for partial months. Also calculate: end-of-contract bonus (if applicable per CBA), completion bonus, and any loyalty/retention payments. Generate final settlement statement showing: final wages, leave pay, bonuses, less advances and deductions, net amount payable. Process payment to crew member's nominated bank account.	\N	ai_agent	\N	\N	\N	"{\\"mode\\":\\"ai_with_tools\\",\\"systemPromptExtra\\":\\"You are a Leave Pay Agent. Calculate leave pay for departing crew — accrued leave, leave pay rate. Provide JSON with: accruedDays, leavePayRate, totalLeavePay, finalSettlement.\\"}"	\N	Leave Pay Calculation AI Agent	4.00	t	\N	\N	system	\N	1	t	"[{\\"field\\":\\"Sign-On/Sign-Off Dates\\",\\"source\\":\\"Step 9 Output\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"SEA/CBA Leave Entitlement Terms\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Leave Taken During Contract\\",\\"source\\":\\"Crew Module\\",\\"required\\":false},{\\"field\\":\\"Basic Wage and Fixed Allowances\\",\\"source\\":\\"Payroll Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Advances and Deductions Register\\",\\"source\\":\\"Payroll Module\\",\\"required\\":true},{\\"field\\":\\"Bonus/Loyalty Payment